            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0390" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg383"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9300: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Linnell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-12T17:00:00+08:00">August 12, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 12—8:18 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following from Ketcham,<anchor n="83" xml:id="d422-f1"/> Swatow.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“August 12, 1 p.m. Japanese Consul is leaving this afternoon. Japanese
                        Consulate turned over to Chinese police for protection. Remaining <pb
                            facs="0391" n="384" xml:id="pg384"/> Japanese are evacuating this
                        afternoon but Japanese Consul informed me about 70 Formosans are remaining
                        in Swatow. Japanese Consul states that his departure is due to increasing
                        anti-Japanese [campaign?] but that Japanese Navy will not take action if
                        Chinese do not attack naval vessels, Japanese subjects or property.
                        Department has not been informed”.</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Sent to the Department, Peiping, Nanking and by mail to Shanghai, Hong Kong,
                    Amoy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Linnell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d422-f1" n="83" xml:id="d422-f1-content">
                <p>John B. Ketcham, Consul at Swatow.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
